      "evidence_points": "The commit message states: \"Because inode_switch_wbs_work_fn() loops when processing isw items, it can happen that wb->switch_work is pending while wb->switch_wbs_ctxs is empty. This is a problem because in that case wb can get freed (no isw items -> no wb reference) while the work is still pending causing use-after-free issues.\" The patch removes the `while (1)` loop, ensuring that the work only processes the items present at the time of its queueing, preventing the list from being emptied prematurely."
